Blur script
File: apps/www-reading-advantage/scripts/blur-tutor-screens.py
It takes --source and --out. It holds one rectangle list per used file. It applies a Gaussian blur
of radius 12 to each rectangle and saves the webp at the delivered size with quality 85. It keeps
the set's folder and file names. It prints each output path. It reads the handoff folder only.
Run: python3 apps/www-reading-advantage/scripts/blur-tutor-screens.py --source
~/Desktop/handoff/a63-tutor-www-calculator/screens --out
apps/www-reading-advantage/public/images/products/tutor-advantage
It printed the three output paths. The three files are 35,422, 17,928, and 65,094 bytes.

Delivered box adjustments (measured, not guessed)
The delivered boxes left glyph pixels outside the blur in four places. A full-size pixel scan found
the glyph bounds, and four edges were widened. The plan records the same four lines.
1. 070 hero x1: 269 to 303. The "3.1" ends at x 301; the delivered box stopped at the "3".
2. 070 bubble y1: 227 to 234. The "g" descender ends at y 232.
3. 062 title x1: 547 to 553. The final "1" ends at x 550 and left a visible stroke.
4. 062 dropdown x0: 391 to 395. The "1:" colon ends at x 392 and must stay.

